          "question": "e-21775",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the first-order linear ODE\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} - 5y = \\cos 2x.\n$$\n\nWe wish to solve this equation using the method of variation of parameters (VOP).\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n$\\qquad$ According to VOP, we assume a particular solution of the form  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044108/assets/ae29bceba4d6a1f250f244b26583abeb4b8c2fbe33d380dfa4332b051bb21078.png).\n\n$\\qquad$ Solving for $u,$ we have $u(x) =$ ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044108/assets/c6725d6cd732c1ca7f21ab9a8dac245bc396c04a623cfb8e2eda31751ddaa89e.png).\n\n$\\qquad$ Therefore, the particular solution is $y_p(x) =$  ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044108/assets/1d1c8a545fb741413f7cdd2f6f3fa6190fbdda74290e206cc4a7f8061f97ff53.png).",
