      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-21775",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution $y_c,$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\ny_c' - 5y_c = 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\ny_c  = Ae^{5x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nThe method of variation of parameters constructs a particular solution by varying the constant in the homogeneous solution. So, to find a suitable $y_p,$ we set $A = u(x)$ in the complementary solution, as given by the following ansatz:\n\n$$\ny_p(x) = u(x)e^{5x}\n$$\n\nIntuitively, this form of $y_p$ tracks the homogeneous solution but with a varying amplitude.\n\nTo find $u,$ we substitute our ansatz into the equation, apply the product rule to the derivative term, and simplify to isolate $u'{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u{e}^{5x})}^{\u2032}-5(u{e}^{5x}) & =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ {u}^{\u2032}{e}^{5x}+5u{e}^{5x}-5u{e}^{5x} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ {u}^{\u2032}{e}^{5x}+\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}}-\\cancel{5u{e}^{5x}} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ {u}^{\u2032}{e}^{5x} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ {u}^{\u2032} & ={e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$ (omitting the arbitrary constant), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{\u2032} & ={e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x \\\\ \\int {u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ u & =\\int {e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $y_p = u(x)e^{5x},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p} & =u(x){e}^{5x} \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {e}^{5x} \\\\  & ={e}^{5x}\\int {e}^{-5x}\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14044108/example-21775.json",
          "file_sha256": "b78cdb5d5674e367e523e06ca3fd1a19425f72274d8b04eaa415f4c988296709"
        }
